  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "119",
  "quote": "A landlord who is lawfully entitled to increase the rent charged to a tenant for a rental unit may do so only if at least 12 months have elapsed",
  "reason": "Section 119(1) requires that at least 12 months elapse before a landlord may increase the rent, setting a minimum waiting period rather than a mandatory requirement to increase rent at 12 months. Agreeing not to increase the rent for the first 24 months satisfies this minimum requirement and is not inconsistent with the Act."
}

